; orca-defaults-x2d.config — the values OrcaSlicer compiles in for settings NO preset file sets.
;
; What it is: 395 `key = value` lines, read by `fdmslice --presets --defaults <this file>` (twobee-fdm, the
; 2bee.fdm engine). They fill ONLY keys the presets left unset (Config::fill_missing), so a preset value always wins.
; Why it exists: Orca fills ~400 keys from PrintConfig.cpp defaults; presets alone lack them and the engine refuses
; on the first one it needs (measured 2026-10-16: "missing config key 'bridge_line_width'").
; Provenance: the CONFIG_BLOCK of a real OrcaSlicer 2.5.0-dev X2D slice (2026-10-16 09:24, print3d-bridge slice
; a61493284e210d34: Bambu Lab X2D 0.4 nozzle + 0.20mm Standard @BBL X2D + Generic PETG @BBL X2D 0.4 nozzle,
; Textured PEI Plate), minus every key those three presets set, minus 24 keys Orca computes PER JOB (left out on
; purpose so the engine cannot inherit that job's value): curr_bed_type default_filament_colour
; different_settings_to_system extruder_ams_count extruder_nozzle_stats filament_colour filament_ids filament_map
; filament_map_2 filament_map_mode filament_nozzle_map filament_self_index filament_volume_map first_layer_bed_temperature
; first_layer_temperature flush_multiplier flush_volumes_matrix flush_volumes_vector inherits_group nozzle_volume_type
; print_compatible_printers wipe_tower_x wipe_tower_y wiping_volumes_extruders.
; ADDED BY HAND 2026-11-12: first_x_layer_fan_speed = 0, from OrcaSlicer main src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
; (set_default_value(new ConfigOptionFloats { 0 })), read as source, not run. The PETG slice above set it in its
; preset, so it was subtracted, and every filament chain that never sets it (checked: Bambu ASA @BBL X2D 0.4) failed in
; layer_change_gcode with FDM-UNRESOLVED. Any other key the PETG preset set has the same hole for other filaments.
; Data, not a program: nothing here runs OrcaSlicer. Regenerating it needs an Orca slice; edit by hand with care.
